{"nodes": [{"id": "shotlist_media_shotlist", "label": "MEDIA_SHOTLIST.md \u2014 media shot list", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "deck/MEDIA_SHOTLIST.md", "source_location": "L1-297", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Day 1 is the bulk of the file (recording-heavy onboarding day). From 2026-09-25 days 2-10 carry recordings too, after the showcase reversal made every section's tasks a recorded demo on the course stack (darrisni)."}, {"id": "shotlist_media_directory", "label": "project-package/slides/media/ \u2014 shared media store", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "deck/MEDIA_SHOTLIST.md", "source_location": "L6", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Trainer records, drops files here with the exact filename, and Claude wires them into the deck."}, {"id": "shotlist_capture_rules", "label": "Capture rules: filenames, PNG/MP4 not GIF, >=1920x1080, light theme", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "deck/MEDIA_SHOTLIST.md", "source_location": "L8-22", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Filenames exact; PNG for a single state, MP4 for any sequence (no audio), never GIF; capture at 1920x1080+ then crop tight; use a clean throwaway account and neutral desktop; never capture a real key/token/password (blur or crop); prefer light OS theme to match the deck's light surfaces."}, {"id": "shotlist_no_secrets_rule", "label": "Never capture a real key, token or password", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "deck/MEDIA_SHOTLIST.md", "source_location": "L19-21", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Bit the project for real once already \u2014 see the context7-redacted.mp4 note; blur or crop the value, the slide only needs to show where the button is."}, {"id": "shotlist_mp4_not_gif", "label": "MP4 not GIF \u2014 drawImage() on an animated GIF returns frame 0", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "deck/MEDIA_SHOTLIST.md", "source_location": "L11-15", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Measured, not assumed: Chromium's drawImage() on an animated GIF returns frame 0 regardless of what's on screen, so a GIF-backed pause button could only ever snap back to its thumbnail. .gifbox now drives a <video>, which stops on the real frame; a box holding a plain <img> hides its pause button rather than lying about pausing."}, {"id": "shotlist_unslotted_shots", "label": "One shot has no slide slot: 04-git-macos-clt.png", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "deck/MEDIA_SHOTLIST.md", "source_location": "L134-140", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Slide 33 covers macOS as one text card (git --version triggers the Xcode Command Line Tools prompt) \u2014 a screenshot doesn't add much a presenter can't just say."}, {"id": "shotlist_graceful_degradation", "label": "Missing shot degrades gracefully to Arabic caption", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "deck/MEDIA_SHOTLIST.md", "source_location": "L293-297", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "media-frame falls back to the step's Arabic caption on a --brand-snow panel, so a missing file leaves a readable slide rather than a broken one."}, {"id": "shotlist_day01", "label": "Day 1 media shot list \u2014 12 slots, all delivered", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "deck/MEDIA_SHOTLIST.md", "source_location": "L24-163", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "day-01.html consumes 12 media slots, reconciled against the built 49-slide deck; most shots delivered as one continuous recording under their own name rather than as the originally planned still-frame placeholders."}, {"id": "shotlist_recordings_merge_slides", "label": "Real recordings collapsed placeholder slides (51->50->47)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "deck/MEDIA_SHOTLIST.md", "source_location": "L39-46,L160", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Several planned still-frame slide pairs turned out better as one continuous recording, so slides merged: e.g. slide 32 merged install+signin; slide 41/42 merged scaffold+running-app; the deck went from 51 to 50 to 47/48 slides across these merges."}, {"id": "shotlist_undocumented_prereqs", "label": "Recordings surfaced undocumented prerequisites", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "deck/MEDIA_SHOTLIST.md", "source_location": "L68-76,L77-91,L152", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Real takes exposed steps no version of the deck or curriculum had documented: the Node.js install gap (github.mp4 shows Claude stalling mid-scaffold), the VS Code 'trust the publisher' prompt, Antigravity's mobile QR verification and possible re-sign-in, and the one-time GitHub Credential Manager 'Authorize' browser step on first push."}, {"id": "shotlist_key_redaction", "label": "context7 key exposure \u2014 gblur redaction 0:56-1:46", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "deck/MEDIA_SHOTLIST.md", "source_location": "L96-102,L220-222", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The raw context7.mp4 shows a real, fully readable API key on screen for ~50s (on context7.com's 'key created' modal, then pasted into chat); redacted with ffmpeg's gblur over exactly that window, verified frame-by-frame. The unredacted file still sits in media/ with the key visible \u2014 flagged for deletion once the key is confirmed revoked. The Day 3 deployment.mp4 note calls this 'the first recording where a real secret reaches the screen' for production keys, with the same blur-in-post discipline."}, {"id": "shotlist_git_setup_reencode", "label": "git-setup.mp4 \u2014 resolution-mismatch reencode", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "deck/MEDIA_SHOTLIST.md", "source_location": "L54-61,L65", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Re-shot identity half is 1080p while the original git.mp4 install half is 720p, so -c copy concat is impossible across the resolution change; git.mp4 alone was upscaled once (scale=1920:1080:flags=lanczos, x264 CRF 18) and the re-shot clip concatenated in untouched, verified by matching four frames byte-for-byte and by exact frame-count arithmetic (1521+1684=3205)."}, {"id": "shotlist_recording_verification_discipline", "label": "Verify against extracted frames, not a transcript summary", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "deck/MEDIA_SHOTLIST.md", "source_location": "L200-222", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An earlier pass reviewed a recording from an auto-generated summary alone and got real things wrong (misattributed who typed a command, invented a prompt, flagged confirmed facts as unconfirmed) \u2014 exactly the mistake the project's own discipline exists to catch; later recordings (Days 4-8) are explicitly frame-verified via ffmpeg trim extraction rather than -ss seek, which was found to mis-time cells via the fps filter's resampling."}, {"id": "shotlist_no_staged_failure_principle", "label": "Do not stage a failure, and do not narrate one that didn't happen", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "deck/MEDIA_SHOTLIST.md", "source_location": "L233-239", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "d4-2 was planned to capture a genuine first-run skill-trigger miss (per Anthropic's guidance that a description is a guess until tested) but the real second session triggered correctly on an unnamed request, so the slide was built to match that footage and the planned 'fix the description' beat was dropped rather than kept as fiction. The honesty principle cuts both ways."}, {"id": "shotlist_shot_06_desktop_usage", "label": "06-desktop-usage.mp4 \u2014 Claude Desktop usage screen", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "deck/MEDIA_SHOTLIST.md", "source_location": "L147", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "slides 22, 31; stepvid with 4 timestamped steps (sidebar -> Settings -> Usage -> read usage bars)."}, {"id": "shotlist_shot_claude_desktop", "label": "claude-desktop.mp4 \u2014 Claude Desktop install+login", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "deck/MEDIA_SHOTLIST.md", "source_location": "L148", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "slide 31."}, {"id": "shotlist_shot_claude_code", "label": "claude-code.mp4 \u2014 Claude Code install, PATH-error fix, sign-in", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "deck/MEDIA_SHOTLIST.md", "source_location": "L149", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "slide 32; one continuous take, 1:19, real PATH-error hiccup and fix, merged install+signin slide."}, {"id": "shotlist_shot_git_setup", "label": "git-setup.mp4 \u2014 Git install + identity setup, joined, 1:46", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "deck/MEDIA_SHOTLIST.md", "source_location": "L150", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "slide 34; joins git.mp4 (install, upscaled to 1080p) and re-shot git-auth.mp4 (identity, 1080p)."}, {"id": "shotlist_shot_antigravity_ide", "label": "antigravity-ide.mp4 \u2014 Antigravity install to Open Folder, 2:00", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "deck/MEDIA_SHOTLIST.md", "source_location": "L151", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "slide 35; surfaced mobile QR verification and a possible second sign-in."}, {"id": "shotlist_shot_claude_code_extension", "label": "claude-code-extension.mp4 \u2014 VS Code extension install + first message, 1:08", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "deck/MEDIA_SHOTLIST.md", "source_location": "L152", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "slide 36; surfaced the 'trust the publisher' prompt; shows the CLAUDE.md day-one greeting logic firing on camera."}, {"id": "shotlist_shot_git_auth_v2", "label": "git-auth.mp4 (re-shot) \u2014 browser-driven Git identity setup, 56.1s", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "deck/MEDIA_SHOTLIST.md", "source_location": "L153", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "slide 34 identity half; trainer's real primary email briefly legible on screen, accepted deliberately (known small audience, intentionally the trainer's real account)."}, {"id": "shotlist_shot_github_auth_superseded", "label": "github-auth.mp4 \u2014 superseded, folded into github.mp4", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "deck/MEDIA_SHOTLIST.md", "source_location": "L154", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No longer needed; the github.mp4 re-recording already shows the real GitHub OAuth authorize page live."}, {"id": "shotlist_shot_node_js", "label": "node-js.mp4 \u2014 Node.js install + verification, 1:55", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "deck/MEDIA_SHOTLIST.md", "source_location": "L77-91,L155", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "slide 37; added because github.mp4 caught Claude stalling mid-scaffold over missing Node.js; steps timed from Gemini's transcript; includes asking Claude to verify and reviewing via conversation_history.md instead of the chat panel."}, {"id": "shotlist_shot_context7_redacted", "label": "context7-redacted.mp4 \u2014 context7 MCP connect, 1:49, blurred", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "deck/MEDIA_SHOTLIST.md", "source_location": "L93-102,L156", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "slide 39; blurred 0:56-1:46 over a real API key; Claude tests the connection with a real doc lookup before confirming."}, {"id": "shotlist_shot_chrome_devtools", "label": "chrome-devtools.mp4 \u2014 chrome-devtools plugin install, 0:29", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "deck/MEDIA_SHOTLIST.md", "source_location": "L92,L157", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "slide 38; shortest of the three Day-1 integrations; the one integration the trainee types themselves because the install command opens an interactive confirmation view an agent's Bash tool can't drive."}, {"id": "shotlist_shot_supabase", "label": "supabase.mp4 \u2014 Supabase project + MCP connect, re-recorded, 3:22", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "deck/MEDIA_SHOTLIST.md", "source_location": "L103-121,L158", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "slide 40; shows the project-brief exchange, Claude proposing the project name (darrisni) and recapping steps, org creation, security-toggle defaults, the one-time MCP trust prompt, and a real table listing to verify."}, {"id": "shotlist_shot_github", "label": "github.mp4 \u2014 create GitHub repo, hand to Claude, plan review, 1:24", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "deck/MEDIA_SHOTLIST.md", "source_location": "L122-132,L159", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "slide 41; caught the missing-Node.js prerequisite and the undocumented GitHub Credential Manager authorize step; three stepvid__fix notes and one stepvid__step--new step added."}, {"id": "shotlist_shot_initial_build", "label": "initial-build.mp4 \u2014 Claude scaffolds, tests, commits, 2:24 edited", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "deck/MEDIA_SHOTLIST.md", "source_location": "L160", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "slide 42 (merged from two old slides); shows chrome-devtools browser automation signing up and checking /dashboard is protected, Claude stopping the server and pushing by itself; 4 stretches sped 3x from 3:15; silent audio dropped."}, {"id": "shotlist_shot_app_running_superseded", "label": "16-app-running.png \u2014 superseded by initial-build.mp4", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "deck/MEDIA_SHOTLIST.md", "source_location": "L161", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "shotlist_shot_first_commit_superseded", "label": "17-first-commit.png \u2014 superseded by push-1.mp4", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "deck/MEDIA_SHOTLIST.md", "source_location": "L162", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "shotlist_shot_push_1", "label": "push-1.mp4 \u2014 verify first commit & push, 0:47", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "deck/MEDIA_SHOTLIST.md", "source_location": "L163", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "slide 43; confirms .env and node_modules excluded, compares editor file tree against the GitHub repo page."}, {"id": "shotlist_shot_tasks_81_82", "label": "tasks-81-82.mp4 \u2014 tasks 8.1+8.2 end to end, 3:24", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "deck/MEDIA_SHOTLIST.md", "source_location": "L180", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Day 2 slide 9; four questions, notebook.txt pasted, Claude returns problem/goal/outcomes without writing to PRODUCT.md first, scope derivation with an explicit two-option gap, approval, commit+push, verified in PRODUCT.md. A real correction round was deliberately cut from the recording."}, {"id": "shotlist_shot_tasks_91_92", "label": "tasks-91-92.mp4 \u2014 tasks 9.1+9.2 in one conversation, 1:49", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "deck/MEDIA_SHOTLIST.md", "source_location": "L182", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Day 2 slide 14; roles table with the stakeholder email line reclassified as an external service; Claude asks a role-overlap question and an ownership assumption; \u00a72 written plus a fourth future-plan item appended."}, {"id": "shotlist_shot_deployment", "label": "deployment.mp4 \u2014 tasks 16.1+16.2 first deploy end to end, 3:22", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "deck/MEDIA_SHOTLIST.md", "source_location": "L195", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Day 3 slide 9; trainer installs the Vercel CLI himself before Claude opens; one browser click to authorize; a one-time MCP trust prompt; first deploy attempt fails and Claude retries successfully from the application folder; self-checked via chrome-devtools; a live login proves the database keys work."}, {"id": "shotlist_shot_task_101", "label": "task-10.1.mp4 \u2014 task 10.1 + FR half of 10.2, 6:16", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "deck/MEDIA_SHOTLIST.md", "source_location": "L196", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Day 3 slide 15; manual /compact in the opening seconds; free-form notes pasted with a deliberate gap left in; Claude returns two conflicts and seven questions unformatted; AskUserQuestion re-framing requested; a third conflict surfaces in plan mode; 32 requirements written; a rendering bug (garbled LTR requirement lines) found and fixed on camera."}, {"id": "shotlist_shot_tasks_103_111_112", "label": "tasks-10.3-11.1-11.2.mp4 \u2014 NFRs + user journey + ERD-adjacent diagram, 5:59", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "deck/MEDIA_SHOTLIST.md", "source_location": "L230", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Day 4 slide 9; seven NFRs with numeric metrics; 22-step unified-format journey; draw.io diagram with a routing-bug self-check and fix; recovers the .drawio source from the PNG's embedded XML, verified byte-identical."}, {"id": "shotlist_shot_task_711", "label": "task-7.11.mp4 \u2014 authoring-skills + skill-creator handoff, 5:30", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "deck/MEDIA_SHOTLIST.md", "source_location": "L231-239", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Day 4 slide 16; six-slot elicitation with suggested answers including a genuine multi-select question; skill-creator writes four files and runs its own with/without comparison against the live site; a second session in Antigravity (not Claude Desktop) triggers the new skill on a plain-language, unnamed request, finds one real finding (404 page not in Arabic), and fixes only that."}, {"id": "shotlist_shot_tasks_12_1_12_2", "label": "tasks_12.1_12.2.mp4 \u2014 screen inventory + identity + commands, 6:23", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "deck/MEDIA_SHOTLIST.md", "source_location": "L248", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Day 5 slide 13; AskUserQuestion live during plan-building; palette from colorhunt.co and Cairo font chosen; PRODUCT.md \u00a75 written and screenshot-verified via chrome-devtools before the trainee reviews it; plan mode into 12.2."}, {"id": "shotlist_shot_tasks_12_3_12_4", "label": "tasks_12.3_12.4.mp4 \u2014 design system + 11 screens generated, 7:06", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "deck/MEDIA_SHOTLIST.md", "source_location": "L249", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Day 5 slide 17; Design System project created, system command pasted, 11 screens generated one conversation at a time; closing batch handoff writes every conversation's name/link into PRODUCT.md \u00a75 at once; verified via rev-parse/ls-remote."}, {"id": "shotlist_shot_tasks_13", "label": "tasks_13.mp4 \u2014 data model extraction + ERD, 4:02", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "deck/MEDIA_SHOTLIST.md", "source_location": "L262", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Day 6 slide 12; one continuous 13.1 pass extracting seven entities, closing four gaps via a multi-tab AskUserQuestion, model written to PRODUCT.md \u00a76, ERD drawn via the drawio skill with its own visual self-check before presenting."}, {"id": "shotlist_shot_task_142", "label": "task_14.2.mp4 \u2014 create DB tables via Supabase MCP, 2:25", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "deck/MEDIA_SHOTLIST.md", "source_location": "L263", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Day 6 slide 17; Claude discovers the Supabase MCP connection needs renewing, explains the blocker plainly, writes the full plan ready to execute, reconnects, then creates all seven tables verified by commit diff and a dashboard browse."}, {"id": "shotlist_shot_task_143", "label": "task_14.3.mp4 \u2014 roles & permissions build, 2:13", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "deck/MEDIA_SHOTLIST.md", "source_location": "L274", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Day 7 slide 10; a Supabase apply_migration call returns declined; Claude investigates rather than retrying blindly, finds it was Supabase's own safety warning for sensitive DDL (not a real rejection), breaks the migration into smaller steps, writes RLS policies per role, tests multiple roles."}, {"id": "shotlist_shot_task_144", "label": "task_14.4.mp4 \u2014 browsing/home page build, documents a design-sync failure, 4:34", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "deck/MEDIA_SHOTLIST.md", "source_location": "L275", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Day 7 slide 16; heavily cut montage (157.3 MiB, gitignored, over GitHub's 100 MiB limit); documents the real /design-sync direction